## Lessons Learned

This sprint introduced the core components of a Security Operations Center (SOC) by centralizing Windows security telemetry into a SIEM.

Key concepts learned include:

- Splunk Enterprise deployment
- Universal Forwarder architecture
- Windows Event Log ingestion
- Sysmon telemetry collection
- Centralized security monitoring
- Log pipeline troubleshooting

The environment is now capable of supporting threat hunting, detection engineering, dashboard creation, and incident response exercises.

---

## Next Sprint

Sprint 7 will focus on building the first SOC dashboards and developing SPL searches for Windows security events, Sysmon telemetry, and PowerShell activity. Detection engineering concepts will be introduced by creating searches for common attacker behaviors and validating them against the collected telemetry.
